// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 22-surface-syntax
// facility: spec/22 §1 str-escape (lexical ill-formedness); inv.str.utf8-validity
// kind: negative
// expect: parse-error
//
// `\x` is a byte-escape, not a str-escape: a str-literal admits no way
// to write an arbitrary byte, which is exactly what keeps its bytes
// well-formed UTF-8 by construction. Using it is a lexical failure.

fn main()
{
    str s = "\x41";
}
